    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Oshkosh-WI/Assistant-Professor-in-Political-Science_JR10015228-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Political Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor in Political Science Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The University of Wisconsin-Oshkosh invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor in Political Science to begin in Fall 2027.  We seek candidates whose primary focus is comparative politics who will thrive in a student-centered environment.  The search is open with respect to regional specialization within the comparative politics subfield.  Affiliated teaching expertise in international relations, law, or policy welcome, but not required.  Candidates must have earned a PhD in Political Science or related discipline by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter.  A record of excellence in teaching is highly desirable.  Key Job Responsibilities: Advise students on academic direction and career opportunities within the field of study Deliver engaging and effective instruction in varied modalities and assess student performance Develop and design curriculum and instructional material reflecting contemporary best practices in pedagogy Mentor students in individual research projects or in pursuit of internship or work experiences. Collaborate closely with faculty and staff across the college to design and implement dynamic, effective teaching strategies that foster student engagement and learning. Provide extensive in-person engagement for students through office hours, advising, and participation in college activities Contribute to the intellectual life of the community and the profession Develop and maintain an active research agenda that contributes to the discipline and enhances the reputation of the program and university. Conduct scholarly research and/or professional work appropriate for tenure Department: School of Public Affairs and Education Compensation: Competitive salary commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: Demonstrated Expertise in Comparative Politics Ability to teach a range of classes contributing to the Political Science Program, including quantitative methodology. Demonstrated scholarly, research, or creative activity appropriate for tenure-track appointment  Commitment to experiential pedagogy and student-centered learning  Ability to work collaboratively in a multidisciplinary academic environment. Preferred Qualifications: Peer-reviewed publications or funded research Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching undergraduate courses and mentoring undergraduate students Education:  Ph.D in Political Science or a closely related field by August 2027 How to Apply: Applicants must submit the following documents using the online application: Letter of application Curriculum vita Teaching statement Research statement Transcripts (official or photocopy) Three current letters of recommendation (can also be sent to recruitment@uwosh.edu) OR contact information for 3 professional references *Please use your application materials to speak to each of the qualifications for this position as listed above. Be sure to describe your relevant experience and areas of expertise, using specific examples from your work and education history. Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required documents prior to submitting the online application. All final candidates will be asked to provide names, email contact information, and/or phone numbers for three (3) references, with at least one being from a manager or supervisor, during the interview process.   Note: Once you have attached your materials and submitted your application, you will not be able to go into the system and change them. To Ensure Consideration: Applications received by the end of the day on 10/20/2026 are ensured full consideration. Applications received after that date may be given consideration. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. Contact Information: For questions regarding your application and additional options to apply, contact Human Resources at recruitment@uwosh.edu or 920-424-1166 Work Authorization Unless otherwise indicated in the job posting, the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. UW Oshkosh is not an e-verify employer; therefore, STEM extensions are not options for work authorization. Legal Notices: Reasonable Accommodations UWO provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities who are employees or applicants for employment. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodations for a qualified individual with a disability. If you need assistance or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact hroffice@uwosh.edu  or 920-424-1166. This job announcement and other material on this site will be made available in alternate formats upon request to an individual with a disability. Confidentiality of Applicant Materials UWO is a State agency and subject to Wisconsin's Open Records Law. UWO will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin's Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \"final candidates\" and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.    CBC & Reference Check Policy All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.    Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) For the UWO Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see https://uwosh.edu/police/ , or call UWO Police Department, at (920) 424-1212 for a paper copy.  UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Oshkosh-WI/Assistant-Professor-in-Special-Education_JR10014939": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Special Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor in Special Education Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The School of Education and Human Services at the University of Wisconsin-Oshkosh invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Special Education beginning in Fall 2027.   We seek a scholar-practitioner with expertise in inclusive special education methods for K–12 learners with disabilities, including curriculum access, assessment-informed instruction, and specially designed instruction. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty committed to preparing future educators through inclusive, equitable, and evidence-based teaching and will contribute to the preparation of educators, counselors, and human service professionals who positively impact schools and communities.  The successful candidate will contribute to teacher preparation in cross-categorical special education, maintain an active program of scholarship, and engage in meaningful service to the university, profession, and community.  This is a 9-month academic year appointment with a standard teaching load of 12 credits per semester. During the first four years of employment, new faculty receive a 3-credit research release each semester, reducing their teaching load to 9 credits per semester while they establish their research and scholarship.  Join us in Oshkosh, WI  Oshkosh, Wisconsin, offers an outstanding quality of life in a vibrant and welcoming community. Nestled along the shores of Lake Winnebago and the Fox River, Oshkosh blends natural beauty with the amenities of city living. Conveniently located just 90 miles from Milwaukee and Madison and 55 miles from Green Bay, residents enjoy easy access to larger metropolitan areas while benefiting from the charm and affordability of a smaller city. Outdoor enthusiasts will find abundant opportunities for hiking, biking, boating, fishing, and other recreational activities nearby. The scenic Northwoods of Wisconsin, picturesque Door County, and the Wisconsin Dells are all within a short drive, making weekend adventures easy and accessible. You can find more information about Oshkosh, WI on the Oshkosh Chamber of Commerce website here.  Key Job Responsibilities: Develop and maintain collaborative partnerships with K–12 schools that support high-quality clinical experiences, program development, and community engagement.   Prepare teacher candidates to use inclusive, evidence-based instructional practices, including explicit instruction, differentiated instruction, assessment-informed decision making, progress monitoring, accommodations, modifications, and IEP-aligned planning.   Prepare future educators to understand and address issues of equity, disability, culture, language, and access to high-quality educational opportunities.   Maintain an active program of scholarship that advances the field of special education and contributes to the mission of the School of Education and Human Services. Teach undergraduate courses in cross-categorical special education with primary emphasis on K–12 methods, literacy, mathematics, curriculum access for learners with mild to moderate disabilities, assessment-informed intervention, specially designed instruction, instructional planning, family engagement and advocacy Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, accreditation, licensure documentation, and continuous program improvement aligned with Wisconsin DPI requirements and CEC standards.   Supervise cross-categorical special education clinical and student teaching experiences, providing coaching and feedback while collaborating with K–12 educators, related service providers, families, and community partners.   Participate in department, college, university, professional, and community service, including recruitment, retention, committee work, and collaborative initiatives.  Develop and teach coursework that prepares teacher candidates to design, implement, and assess evidence-based instruction for learners with disabilities across elementary, middle, and secondary settings.  Advise and mentor teacher candidates throughout their educator preparation program.   Department: School of Education and Human Services Compensation: Competitive c ommensurate with experience Required Qualifications: Earned doctorate or ABD in Special Education, Curriculum and Instruction with a special education emphasis, Learning Disabilities, or a closely related field.   Demonstrated expertise in accessible special education methods for K–12 learners with disabilities, including literacy, mathematics, curriculum access, assessment-informed instruction, and specially designed instruction.   Minimum of three years of successful professional experience in K–12 cross-categorical special education.   Eligibility for, or equivalent preparation aligned with, cross-categorical special education licensure, including the ability to teach and supervise teacher candidates in coursework, clinical experiences, and student teaching.   Evidence of an active program of scholarship or the potential to develop a sustained research agenda related to special education.   Demonstrated commitment to accessible practices, culturally responsive teaching, collaboration, equitable access to the general curriculum, and the preparation of future educators to support students with disabilities.   Preferred Qualifications: Successful K–12 teaching experience in cross-categorical special education, particularly in elementary, middle, and/or secondary settings serving students with learning disabilities, emotional or behavioral disabilities, intellectual disabilities, autism, and other disabilities.   Demonstrated expertise in evidence-based literacy assessment and instruction for students with disabilities, including intervention planning and progress monitoring.   Experience teaching or the ability to teach augmentative communication (AC). Experience teaching special education methods, curriculum, assessment, IEP development, instructional planning, or specially designed instruction in a teacher preparation program.   Experience supervising teacher candidates during clinical placements or student teaching in K–12 special education settings.   Knowledge of CEC special educator preparation standards, Wisconsin DPI licensure and program requirements, evidence-based instructional practices, and collaborative service delivery.   Evidence of school partnerships, curriculum leadership, program assessment, or other leadership experiences related to special education.  Education: Minimum Degree Required: Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Special Education, Curriculum and Instruction, or a closely related field (ABD considered with completion by appointment date).  How to Apply: Applicants must submit the following documents using the online application: Letter of interest addressing qualifications and fit for the position.   Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Research statement describing current and future scholarly agenda Three professional letters of reference Applicants should address the required and preferred qualifications throughout their application materials using specific examples from their teaching, scholarship, leadership, and professional experiences.  Applicants are encouraged to describe their philosophy of preparing future educators to support students with disabilities through inclusive, evidence-based, accessible, and culturally responsive practices. Statements may also address experience teaching in environments that support belonging for all learners; the ability to prepare future educators who understand disability studies perspectives and promote equal access to education, employment, and full adult life for individuals across the disability spectrum; knowledge of disproportionality in special education and its impact on students, families, schools, and communities; and a commitment to advancing equitable educational opportunities for learners from multifaceted backgrounds and identities.  All final candidates will be asked to provide names, email contact information, and/or phone numbers for three (3) references, with at least one being from a manager or supervisor, during the interview process.   Note: Once you have attached your materials and submitted your application, you will not be able to go into the system and change them. To Ensure Consideration: Applications received by the end of the day on 10/4/2026 are ensured full consideration. Applications received after that date may be given consideration. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. Contact Information: For questions regarding your application and additional options to apply, contact Human Resources at recruitment@uwosh.edu or 920-424-1166 Work Authorization Unless otherwise indicated in the job posting, the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. UW Oshkosh is not an e-verify employer; therefore, STEM extensions are not options for work authorization. Legal Notices: Reasonable Accommodations UWO provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities who are employees or applicants for employment. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodations for a qualified individual with a disability. If you need assistance or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact hroffice@uwosh.edu  or 920-424-1166. This job announcement and other material on this site will be made available in alternate formats upon request to an individual with a disability. Confidentiality of Applicant Materials UWO is a State agency and subject to Wisconsin's Open Records Law. UWO will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin's Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \"final candidates\" and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.    CBC & Reference Check Policy All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.    Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) For the UWO Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see https://uwosh.edu/police/ , or call UWO Police Department, at (920) 424-1212 for a paper copy.  UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Oshkosh-WI/Learning-Technology-Specialist-and-Mobile-Simulation-Lab-Operator-Driver_JR10014190": {
      "title": "Learning Technology Specialist and Mobile Simulation Lab Operator/Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Learning Technology Specialist and Mobile Simulation Lab Operator/Driver Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Teaching, Learning, and Technology Specialist I Job Duties: The University of Wisconsin Oshkosh is seeking a Learning Technology Specialist and Mobile Simulation Lab Operator/Driver to support the READY RURAL initiative and its innovative mobile healthcare simulation program. This unique position combines safe operation and transportation of the READY RURAL Mobile Simulation Lab with hands-on simulation and learning technology support in rural communities. As a key member of the READY RURAL team, the majority of your work while on site will focus on supporting simulation activities, including setting up and operating simulation equipment, telehealth and Virtual Care technology, audiovisual systems, and other instructional technologies. You will work directly with faculty, staff, learners, healthcare partners, and workforce participants to ensure mobile simulation experiences are ready, accessible, and technically supported. The position will also be responsible for safely driving and transporting the Mobile Simulation Lab to campus, healthcare, school, community, and rural partner locations. Responsibilities include conducting vehicle and equipment inspections, maintaining transportation and deployment records, coordinating basic site logistics, and ensuring equipment is safely loaded, secured, and ready for deployment. Additional responsibilities include maintaining inventories, inspecting and cleaning simulation equipment, troubleshooting basic technology issues, documenting equipment readiness, and identifying maintenance or supply needs. The successful candidate will bring strong attention to detail, a commitment to safety, comfort working with technology and equipment, and the ability to provide excellent hands-on support in a variety of field-based environments. Universities of Wisconsin also offers an extremely competitive benefits package for 2026 that includes: Health plans, currently starting at $45 per month. 176 hours of vacation per year (prorated for start date). 36 hours of personal holiday, and 9 legal holidays (prorated for start date). 176 Hours of sick leave for first 18 months. After this period, employees can earn up to 96 hours per fiscal year. Accumulates without limit and does not expire. Paid parental leave after six months of continuous employment. Wisconsin Retirement System (pension) with 7.2% employer contribution for 2026. All employment benefits are subject to change. A full list of current benefits and eligibility requirements can be found on our website. This position is funded through the READY RURAL grant and is initially offered as a one-year fixed-term appointment. The appointment is renewable annually for up to four years, contingent upon continued grant funding, satisfactory performance, and program needs. Key Job Responsibilities: Assists with the design and development of multimedia learning materials Assists with providing basic training and technical support to learners in settings such as classrooms, labs, clinics, and distance learning mediums Provides support for faculty development and engagement programs and activities Assists with the design and development of engaging, effective learning experiences which may be face-to-face, blended, and/or online Provides support for collecting, organizing, interpreting, and disseminating data to identify instructional program needs and enhance effectiveness Contributes to researching, designing, and/or acquiring learning resources, technologies, materials, and/or processes to support learning Provides consultation, training, and/or support for learning technology tools and platforms Completes initial edits, reviews, and updates of existing instructional materials Analyzes, tests, troubleshoots, resolves issues, and provides feedback regarding learning technologies Department: School of Nursing and Health Professions Compensation: Starting at $53,000 commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: ​ Bachelor’s degree in instructional technology, educational technology, information technology, healthcare technology, simulation operations, transportation, logistics, or related field. Valid Wisconsin driver’s license and eligible to be an authorized driver through UW System. Experience operating vehicles, trailers, RVs, service vehicles, mobile units, or related equipment. Experience setting up, maintaining, or troubleshooting equipment, technology, audiovisual tools, healthcare training equipment, or instructional technology. Ability to lift, move, load, unload, and set up equipment weighing up to 50 pounds with or without reasonable accommodations. Ability to travel throughout Wisconsin and work occasional evening, weekend, or overnight deployment schedules as needed. Preferred Qualifications: Experience supporting simulation-based education, telehealth, Virtual Care, remote patient monitoring, audiovisual systems, learning technology, or mobile training environments. Experience providing technical support to learners, faculty, instructors, or end users. Experience with inventory systems, asset tracking, vehicle maintenance coordination, or equipment lifecycle documentation. Commercial Driver’s License or experience driving specialty vehicles, mobile labs, trailers, or large service vehicles. How to Apply: Applicants must submit the following documents using the online application: Resume Cover Letter *Please use your application materials to speak to each of the qualifications for this position as listed above. Be sure to describe your relevant experience and areas of expertise, using specific examples from your work and education history. Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required documents prior to submitting the online application. All final candidates will be asked to provide names, email contact information, and/or phone numbers for three (3) references, with at least one being from a manager or supervisor, during the interview process.   Note: Once you have attached your materials and submitted your application, you will not be able to go into the system and change them. To Ensure Consideration: Applications received by the end of the day on 09/16/2026 are ensured full consideration.   Applications received after that date may be given consideration. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. Contact Information: For questions regarding your application and additional options to apply, contact Human Resources at recruitment@uwosh.edu or 920-424-1166 Work Authorization Unless otherwise indicated in the job posting, the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. UW Oshkosh is not an e-verify employer; therefore, STEM extensions are not options for work authorization. Legal Notices: Reasonable Accommodations UWO provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities who are employees or applicants for employment. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodations for a qualified individual with a disability. If you need assistance or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact hroffice@uwosh.edu  or 920-424-1166. This job announcement and other material on this site will be made available in alternate formats upon request to an individual with a disability. Confidentiality of Applicant Materials UWO is a State agency and subject to Wisconsin's Open Records Law. UWO will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin's Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \"final candidates\" and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.    CBC & Reference Check Policy All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.    Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) For the UWO Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see https://uwosh.edu/police/ , or call UWO Police Department, at (920) 424-1212 for a paper copy.  UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Oshkosh-WI/Assistant--Associate--Full-Professor--Computer-Science_JR10013727": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, Full Professor- Computer Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant, Associate, Full Professor- Computer Science Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Computer Science Department at the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh seeks applicants for a tenure-track Computer Science position beginning in Spring or Fall 2027. Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field is required. ABDs with a reasonable likelihood of degree completion prior to hiring may also apply. Duties include teaching in an ABET-accredited program, conducting research, advising majors and serving on a variety of committees. Applicants must submit all of the following materials: letter of application, curriculum vita, teaching statement, research statement, transcripts (official or photocopy), and three current letters of recommendation OR contact information for 3 professional references. A regional comprehensive university committed to the teacher/scholar model; the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh is part of the robust Universities of Wisconsin system - one of the largest systems of public higher education in the country. UW Oshkosh proudly serves the northeast Fox valley region in Wisconsin with an annual on- and off-campus enrollment of nearly 10,000. An emphasis in teaching excellence is the hallmark of all Universities of Wisconsin campuses. We are committed to delivering a high-quality education and a strong foundation for those who wish to pursue professional, occupational, and advanced academic degrees. Our students are a mix of traditional and non-traditional age, including many first-generation college students. The University of Wisconsin Oshkosh is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Join Us in Oshkosh, WI! Oshkosh, Wisconsin offers an outstanding quality of life in a vibrant and welcoming community. Nestled along the shores of Lake Winnebago and the Fox River, Oshkosh combines nature with city living.  The city also hosts world-renowned events such as EAA AirVenture, the world’s largest aviation gathering. The Fox Valley offers a nice combination of amenities and relatively low cost of living and is within driving distance of Milwaukee, Madison, Chicago, and Minneapolis-St. Paul, offering easy access to major cities while retaining the convenience of a smaller community. You can find more information about Oshkosh, WI on the Oshkosh Chamber of Commerce website here . Key Job Responsibilities: Department: School of STEM Compensation: Starting at $85,000 commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: An earned Ph.D in Computer Science or closely related field. ABDs may apply but must have earned degree by start date. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated record of effective teaching, or evidence of strong potential for effective teaching, as demonstrated through teaching experience, student evaluations (if available), teaching awards, a teaching statement, etc. Evidence of the ability and willingness to teach a variety of undergraduate Computer Science courses, as demonstrated through prior teaching experience, graduate coursework, a statement of teaching interests, etc. Record of scholarly activity demonstrated by publications in refereed journals and/or peer-reviewed conference proceedings. Demonstrated expertise or specialization in one or more of the following areas, as evidenced by education, research, publications, professional experience, or teaching: Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, or Intelligent, Agentic, and Secure Systems. Evidence of the ability and willingness to teach in multiple instructional modalities (e.g., face-to-face, online, and hybrid) and/or teach graduate-level Computer Science courses, as demonstrated through prior teaching experience or a statement of teaching interests. How to Apply: Applicants must submit the following documents using the online application: Letter of application Curriculum vita Teaching statement Research statement Transcripts (official or photocopy) Three current letters of recommendation (can also be sent to recruitment@uwosh.edu ) OR contact information for 3 professional references *Please use your application materials to speak to each of the qualifications for this position as listed above. Be sure to describe your relevant experience and areas of expertise, using specific examples from your work and education history. Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required documents prior to submitting the online application. Note: Once you have attached your materials and submitted your application, you will not be able to go into the system and change them. To Ensure Consideration: Applications received by the end of the day on 10/09/2026 are ensured full consideration.   Applications received after that date may be given consideration. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. Contact Information: For questions regarding your application and additional options to apply, contact Human Resources at recruitment@uwosh.edu or 920-424-1166 Work Authorization Unless otherwise indicated in the job posting, the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. UW Oshkosh is not an e-verify employer; therefore, STEM extensions are not options for work authorization. Legal Notices: Reasonable Accommodations UWO provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities who are employees or applicants for employment. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodations for a qualified individual with a disability. If you need assistance or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact hroffice@uwosh.edu  or 920-424-1166. This job announcement and other material on this site will be made available in alternate formats upon request to an individual with a disability. Confidentiality of Applicant Materials UWO is a State agency and subject to Wisconsin's Open Records Law. UWO will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin's Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \"final candidates\" and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.    CBC & Reference Check Policy All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.    Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) For the UWO Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see https://uwosh.edu/police/ , or call UWO Police Department, at (920) 424-1212 for a paper copy.  UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Oshkosh-WI/Assistant-Director-of-Simulation_JR10013689": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Simulation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Director of Simulation Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Academic Assessment Manager Job Duties: Join the READY RURAL team and play a key leadership role in advancing innovative, simulation-based healthcare education that prepares learners for today's evolving workforce. The Assistant Director of Simulation provides leadership for simulation strategy, academic assessment, technology integration, faculty development, and competency-based evaluation across READY RURAL's simulation and Virtual Care-enabled learning environments. In this collaborative leadership role, you will work closely with faculty, healthcare partners, and campus stakeholders to ensure simulation experiences are aligned with curricular outcomes, professional competencies, accreditation standards, workforce needs, and grant objectives. You will help shape and coordinate simulation initiatives, oversee assessment and quality assurance processes, support technology-enabled learning, and provide consultation and professional development that promotes excellence in simulation-based education. The Assistant Director will coordinate simulation operations, including lab and Virtual Care scheduling, equipment readiness, and technology integration, while supporting innovative teaching, competency tracking, learner assessment, and outcomes reporting. This position also plays a vital role in collecting and analyzing data for grant reporting, accreditation, continuous quality improvement, and workforce readiness initiatives. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced educational leader who is passionate about advancing healthcare education through simulation, evidence-based instructional practices, academic assessment, and collaborative partnerships that strengthen student success and rural healthcare workforce development. Universities of Wisconsin also offers an extremely competitive benefits package for 2026 that includes: Health plans, currently starting at $45 per month. 176 hours of vacation per year (prorated for start date). 36 hours of personal holiday, and 9 legal holidays (prorated for start date). 176 Hours of sick leave for first 18 months. After this period, employees can earn up to 96 hours per fiscal year. Accumulates without limit and does not expire. Paid parental leave after six months of continuous employment. Wisconsin Retirement System (pension) with 7.2% employer contribution for 2026. All employment benefits are subject to change. A full list of current benefits and eligibility requirements can be found on our website. This position is funded through the READY RURAL grant and is initially offered as a one-year fixed-term appointment. Opportunity for renewal past the initial year is possible depending on grant funding and satisfactory performance. Key Job Responsibilities: Plans, executes, and evaluates data collection initiatives, and maintains management and collection resources Serves as a subject matter expert and liaison to internal and external stakeholders Collects, prepares, and analyzes data, and prepares reports Continuously improves methods and processes for assessment instrument development Manages complex databases and performs analyses of large data sets May exercise supervisory authority, including hiring, transferring, suspending, promoting, managing conduct and performance, discharging, assigning, rewarding, disciplining, and/or approving hours worked of at least 2.0 FTE or equivalent employees Provides operational guidance on the implementation of new or revised institutional operational policies and procedures for learning and programmatic assessment Department: College of Nursing, Health Professions and STEM Compensation: Starting at $85,000 commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Healthcare, Education, Assessment, Curriculum and Instruction, Instructional Technology, Health Sciences, Nursing, Public Health, or related field Experience coordinating academic programs, assessment activities, simulation programs, curriculum initiatives, or teaching and learning support services. Experience supporting assessment planning, data collection, reporting, accreditation, program review, or quality improvement activities. Experience working collaboratively with faculty, academic programs, staff, and internal or external stakeholders. Strong communication, consultation, organization, and analytical skills. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in Healthcare Education, Assessment, Curriculum and Instruction, Nursing, Health Sciences, Educational Technology, Public Health, or related field. Experience in healthcare simulation, Virtual Care, telehealth education, interprofessional education, or competency-based education. Experience with accreditation processes in nursing, health professions, healthcare simulation, or higher education. Experience using assessment management systems, learning management systems, simulation management systems, dashboards, or data visualization tools. Simulation certification or relevant training such as CHSE, CHSOS, or equivalent experience. How to Apply: Applicants must submit the following documents using the online application: Resume Cover Letter *Please use your application materials to speak to each of the qualifications for this position as listed above. Be sure to describe your relevant experience and areas of expertise, using specific examples from your work and education history. Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required documents prior to submitting the online application. All final candidates will be asked to provide names, email contact information, and/or phone numbers for three (3) references, with at least one being from a manager or supervisor, during the interview process.   Note: Once you have attached your materials and submitted your application, you will not be able to go into the system and change them. To Ensure Consideration: Applications received by the end of the day on 8/24/2026 are ensured full consideration.   Applications received after that date may be given consideration. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. Contact Information: For questions regarding your application and additional options to apply, contact Human Resources at recruitment@uwosh.edu or 920-424-1166 Work Authorization Unless otherwise indicated in the job posting, the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. UW Oshkosh is not an e-verify employer; therefore, STEM extensions are not options for work authorization. Legal Notices: Reasonable Accommodations UWO provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities who are employees or applicants for employment. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodations for a qualified individual with a disability. If you need assistance or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact hroffice@uwosh.edu  or 920-424-1166. This job announcement and other material on this site will be made available in alternate formats upon request to an individual with a disability. Confidentiality of Applicant Materials UWO is a State agency and subject to Wisconsin's Open Records Law. UWO will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin's Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \"final candidates\" and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.    CBC & Reference Check Policy All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.    Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) For the UWO Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see https://uwosh.edu/police/ , or call UWO Police Department, at (920) 424-1212 for a paper copy.  UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Oshkosh-WI/Instructional-Designer---Learning-Technology-Specialist_JR10013688": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer & Learning Technology Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructional Designer & Learning Technology Specialist Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Instructional and Media Designer Job Duties: The University of Wisconsin Oshkosh is seeking a collaborative and innovative Instructional Designer & Learning Technology Specialist to support the READY RURAL initiative. This position serves as the lead for instructional design, educational technology, digital learning, and multimedia development, partnering with faculty and subject matter experts to transform content into engaging, accessible, and workforce-focused learning experiences. In this role, you will design and develop high-quality instructional materials for online, hybrid, face-to-face, simulation, mobile, and partner-based learning environments. You will create innovative learning resources that support rural healthcare education, including topics such as telehealth, virtual care, remote patient monitoring, behavioral health, home-based care, interprofessional practice, care coordination, and workforce readiness. The position also supports the development of stackable credentials, continuing education offerings, faculty development resources, and workforce training programs. The successful candidate will provide consultation and support to faculty and staff on instructional technologies, digital learning tools, accessibility, and inclusive teaching practices. Responsibilities include developing multimedia resources such as instructional videos, simulations, interactive learning modules, digital toolkits, and tutorials, while ensuring all learning materials meet quality and accessibility standards. This position also plays a key role in managing instructional design and media development projects by coordinating timelines, maintaining documentation and reusable resources, training faculty and project personnel on educational technologies, and supporting the collection and interpretation of data to continuously improve learning experiences and program effectiveness. Universities of Wisconsin also offers an extremely competitive benefits package for 2026 that includes: Health plans, currently starting at $45 per month. 176 hours of vacation per year (prorated for start date). 36 hours of personal holiday, and 9 legal holidays (prorated for start date). 176 Hours of sick leave for first 18 months. After this period, employees can earn up to 96 hours per fiscal year. Accumulates without limit and does not expire. Paid parental leave after six months of continuous employment. Wisconsin Retirement System (pension) with 7.2% employer contribution for 2026. All employment benefits are subject to change. A full list of current benefits and eligibility requirements can be found on our website. This position is funded through the READY RURAL grant and is initially offered as a one-year fixed-term appointment. The appointment is renewable annually for up to four years, contingent upon continued grant funding, satisfactory performance, and program needs. Key Job Responsibilities: Applies project management principles to course or media design such as defining project scope, establishing milestones, and tracking progress Provides pedagogical consultation services for instructors and staff on instructional toolsand technologies, best practices for digital instructional content, and institutional initiatives Establishes and maintains collaborative relationships with instructors and other academic staff to advance excellence in teaching and learning Reviews courses, media, or other learning products for quality using industry standardsand accessibility best practices Trains and supports instructors and staff to leverage technology and teach implement pedagogy effectively Works with campus partners across pre-production, production, and post-production stages of media development for implementation in courses and other campusinitiatives Creates and maintains documentation on pedagogy, course or media design, templates, instructional technologies, and curates a library of shareable resources Designs and develops learning activities and course content using instructional technologies to foster inclusive and equitable student experiences Department: College of Nursing, Health Professions and STEM Compensation: Starting at $60,000 commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Instructional Design, Educational Technology, Curriculum and Instruction, Learning Design, Media Production, Healthcare Education, or related field Experience designing online, hybrid, technology-enhanced, or multimedia learning experiences. Experience with learning management systems, digital learning tools, instructional technologies, or media production tools. Experience consulting with faculty, instructors, trainers, or subject matter experts. Strong project management, communication, organization, and technical problem-solving skills. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in instructional design, educational technology, learning sciences, curriculum and instruction, healthcare education, or related field. Experience supporting healthcare education, simulation-based education, workforce development, continuing education, or academic-practice training. Experience with tools such as Canvas, Articulate 360, Adobe Creative Cloud, Camtasia, H5P, video platforms, virtual simulation tools, or similar systems. Experience with accessibility standards, Universal Design for Learning, inclusive pedagogy, and AI-assisted instructional design. Experience supporting telehealth, digital health, Virtual Care, or simulation learning environments. How to Apply: Applicants must submit the following documents using the online application: Resume Cover Letter *Please use your application materials to speak to each of the qualifications for this position as listed above. Be sure to describe your relevant experience and areas of expertise, using specific examples from your work and education history. Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required documents prior to submitting the online application. All final candidates will be asked to provide names, email contact information, and/or phone numbers for three (3) references, with at least one being from a manager or supervisor, during the interview process.   Note: Once you have attached your materials and submitted your application, you will not be able to go into the system and change them. To Ensure Consideration: Applications received by the end of the day on 8/24/2026 are ensured full consideration.   Applications received after that date may be given consideration. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. Contact Information: For questions regarding your application and additional options to apply, contact Human Resources at recruitment@uwosh.edu or 920-424-1166 Work Authorization Unless otherwise indicated in the job posting, the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. UW Oshkosh is not an e-verify employer; therefore, STEM extensions are not options for work authorization. Legal Notices: Reasonable Accommodations UWO provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities who are employees or applicants for employment. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodations for a qualified individual with a disability. If you need assistance or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact hroffice@uwosh.edu  or 920-424-1166. This job announcement and other material on this site will be made available in alternate formats upon request to an individual with a disability. Confidentiality of Applicant Materials UWO is a State agency and subject to Wisconsin's Open Records Law. UWO will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin's Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \"final candidates\" and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.    CBC & Reference Check Policy All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.    Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) For the UWO Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see https://uwosh.edu/police/ , or call UWO Police Department, at (920) 424-1212 for a paper copy.  UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Oshkosh-WI/Assistant--Associate-or-Full-Professor---Nursing_JR10013658": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor - Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-04\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant, Associate or Full Professor - Nursing Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The School of Nursing and Health Professions (SoNHP) at the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh invites applications for tenure-track Assistant/Associate/Full Professor positions with anticipated start date in Spring 2027. To fill these faculty positions, we are seeking candidates who are collaborative, energetic, and have expertise in nursing education and/or advanced practice nursing (nurse practitioner). Responsibilities include teaching, scholarship, and service. Rank will be determined upon review of qualifications. About Us: Our mission in the School of Nursing and Health Professions empowers students, faculty and staff to advance physical and emotional well-being in all communities through education, research, and practice. By fostering critical thinking, ethical leadership, and evidence-based expertise, we prepare future professionals to lead with compassion, inclusiveness, and innovation in an ever-evolving world. You can find more information about the School of Nursing and Health Professions on our website  here .  Join Us in Oshkosh, WI! Oshkosh, Wisconsin offers an outstanding quality of life in a vibrant and welcoming community. Nestled along the shores of Lake Winnebago and the Fox River, Oshkosh combines nature with city living.  The city also hosts world-renowned events such as EAA AirVenture, the world’s largest aviation gathering. Oshkosh is conveniently located about 90 minutes from Milwaukee and Madison, and just 45 minutes from Green Bay, offering easy access to major cities while retaining the convenience of a smaller community. You can find more information about Oshkosh, WI on the Oshkosh Chamber of Commerce website  here . Key Job Responsibilities: Scholarship Perform campus, community, and professional service Teaching Department: School of Nursing and Health Professions Compensation: C ompetitive, commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited nursing program associated with a regionally accredited institution of higher education Doctoral degree (PhD, DNP) appropriate to content area or near degree completion (final semester) If advanced practice nurse practitioner applicant, must be eligible for national certification in advanced practice and/or recertification eligible with ANCC or AANP. Unencumbered license as a registered nurse and/or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse and eligible for licensure in the state of Wisconsin Five or more years of clinical nursing experience Preferred Qualifications: Undergraduate and Graduate level teaching experience Distance/online teaching experience Evidence of scholarship and service How to Apply: Applicants must submit the following documents using the online application: Letter of intent Curriculum vita Official transcripts from undergraduate and graduate programs including doctoral education Contact information for three professional references Two letters of recommendation upon request *Please use your application materials to speak to each of the qualifications for this position as listed above. Be sure to describe your relevant experience and areas of expertise, using specific examples from your work and education history. Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required documents prior to submitting the online application. All final candidates will be asked to provide names, email contact information, and/or phone numbers for three (3) references, with at least one being from a manager or supervisor, during the interview process.   Note: Once you have attached your materials and submitted your application, you will not be able to go into the system and change them.   To Ensure Consideration: Applications received by the end of the day on 10/31/2026 are ensured full consideration. Applications received after that date may be given consideration at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated and qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete application materials may not receive consideration. Contact Information: For questions regarding your application and additional options to apply, contact Human Resources at recruitment@uwosh.edu or 920-424-1166 Work Authorization Unless otherwise indicated in the job posting, the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. UW Oshkosh is not an e-verify employer; therefore, STEM extensions are not options for work authorization.  Legal Notices: Reasonable Accommodations UWO provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities who are employees or applicants for employment. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodations for a qualified individual with a disability. If you need assistance or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact hroffice@uwosh.edu  or 920-424-1166. This job announcement and other material on this site will be made available in alternate formats upon request to an individual with a disability. Confidentiality of Applicant Materials UWO is a State agency and subject to Wisconsin's Open Records Law. UWO will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin's Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \"final candidates\" and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.    CBC & Reference Check Policy All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.    Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) For the UWO Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see https://uwosh.edu/police/ , or call UWO Police Department, at (920) 424-1212 for a paper copy.  UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Oshkosh-WI/Head-Start-Early-Childhood-Education-Assistant-Teacher--Continuous-Recruitment-_JR10012644": {
      "title": "Head Start Early Childhood Education Assistant Teacher (Continuous Recruitment)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-01\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Head Start Early Childhood Education Assistant Teacher (Continuous Recruitment) Job Category: University Staff Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Early Child Edu Asst Teacher Job Duties: Early Childhood Education Assistant Teachers will work within the UW Oshkosh Head Start program, which is a federally funded, preschool program for low-income families.   Each position works collaboratively to develop skills and practices to support school readiness for each child and to support our comprehensive services offered to each child and family.  Classroom sizes are 15-16 children.  School is in session September – May/early June, with additional August work hours for staff.  Our program embraces the High/Scope curriculum, offers many professional development opportunities, and implements Pyramid Model and Conscious Discipline programs to support social/emotional development.  Head Start employees have the opportunity to work with 384 children and their families every school year. We have seven centers in five different cities throughout Winnebago, Calumet, Outagamie, and Shawano Counties.   Staff wellness is prioritized through available individual/group reflective practice, Practice Based Coaching, and wellness initiatives.  Key Job Responsibilities: Maintains the safety and physical well-being of children in a designated classroom Assists with basic technical and administrative classroom support Documents effective communication with internal and external stakeholders to relay pertinent information and provide updates of child activities per established guidelines and regulations Updates and organizes individualized and developmental educational plans for children Assists with the planning and facilitation of classroom programming and classroom coordination and organization for a early childhood education facility according to established curriculums Department: Head Start Compensation: $17.37 - $19.50 per hour Required Qualifications: Completed or current enrollment in an Associate Degree in Early Childhood Education program or a Preschool Child Development Associate Credential (CDA). If currently enrolled in either program they must be successfully completed within 9 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelors Degree in Early Childhood Education How to Apply: To apply, click on the APPLY button or go to: http://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives?Institution=5adf054562b610142325cb73e24d0000 Required application materials : Resume Unofficial Transcripts * Please use your application materials to speak to each of the qualifications for this position as listed above. Be sure to describe your relevant experience and areas of expertise, using specific examples from your work and education history. All final candidates will be asked to provide names, email contact information, and/or phone numbers for three (3) references, with at least one being from a manager or supervisor, during the interview process.    Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required documents prior to submitting the online application. Note: Once you have attached your materials and submitted your application you will not be able to go into the system and change them. Contact Information: For questions regarding your application and additional options to apply: Contact Human Resources at recruitment@uwosh.edu  or 920-424-1166. Legal Notices: Reasonable Accommodations UWO provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities who are employees or applicants for employment. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodations for a qualified individual with a disability. If you need assistance or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact hroffice@uwosh.edu  or 920-424-1166. This job announcement and other material on this site will be made available in alternate formats upon request to an individual with a disability. Confidentiality of Applicant Materials UWO is a State agency and subject to Wisconsin's Open Records Law. UWO will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin's Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \"final candidates\" and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.    CBC & Reference Check Policy All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.    Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) For the UWO Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see https://uwosh.edu/police/ , or call UWO Police Department, at (920) 424-1212 for a paper copy.  UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
